      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This report describes the case of a giant aneurysmal right coronary artery connecting to the coronary sinus near its opening into the right atrium in a 70-year-old woman who presented with a recent onset of congestive heart failure. By coincidence, a secundum atrial septal defect was also present. The diagnosis and surgical management of this uncommon pathology are described."},
